{"op":"pr_create","title":"feat(mail): IMAP polling per contract folder, durable seen-marker, alert-surfaced outages","base":"main","head":"feat/imap-polling","body":"Closes #84.\n\nExtends the existing IMAP client built for the Sent-folder append (#72) rather than adding a second IMAP stack, per the issue's own instruction.\n\n## What this does\n\n- `contract.mail_folder` (nullable text): the IMAP folder or Gmail label a contract's incoming approval mail is filed under, in the same account `IMAP_HOST`/`IMAP_USER` already authenticate to. Set from the mail hub (`/mail/contracts/[id]`, a new form next to the existing auto-send and template-language settings, same narrow-setter shape as `setContractAutoSendMail`/`setContractTemplateLanguage`). At most one contract can claim a folder (`contract_mail_folder_key`).\n- `inbound_thread`: one row per message handed off. Carries `contractId` directly (#84's acceptance: \"each handed-off thread carries the contract id its folder/label maps to\") plus `documentId` pointing at the archived raw `.eml` (`document`, `provenance: 'mail'`, owned by the contract itself the same way `createApproval` starts a freshly archived original before anything downstream decides what it evidences — there is no `approval` row yet at ingestion time). This table **is** the hand-off; nothing reads it yet in this wave (confirmed with the #82 agent: the runner's DB role is read-only on `contract`/`document` only, no queue table on its side), so whoever wires #85 next reads pending rows here and invokes the runner with `{documentId, contractId}`.\n- The durable seen-marker is a database-enforced unique index on `(contract_id, imap_uid_validity, imap_uid)` — IMAP UIDs are stable per mailbox only within one `UIDVALIDITY` generation, so the poller's cursor query is always scoped to the mailbox's *current* `UIDVALIDITY`. A second unique index on `(contract_id, message_id)` (partial, message-id not always present) is the safety net for a `UIDVALIDITY` bump specifically: a message re-numbered under a new generation still carries the same `Message-ID`, so it is recognised as already handed off rather than reprocessed. Both are proven against a real, forced `UIDVALIDITY` bump on GreenMail (delete the mailbox, wait past GreenMail's time-derived validity tick, recreate it), not just asserted at the schema level.\n- `mailbox_poll_run`: one row per poll pass, same shape as `backup_run`/`document_mirror_run` (this issue's own instruction — reuse that pattern, don't invent a third). A connection failure is retried with exponential backoff (`connectWithRetry`, 5 attempts by default, `500ms/1s/2s/4s`) before the pass gives up and records `failure`; a folder-specific problem (deleted/renamed mailbox) is captured per-folder without blocking any other contract's folder in the same pass. Surfaced through the alert engine as a new `mailbox_poll_failure` type, gated on IMAP actually being configured *and* at least one contract having a folder mapped — the same \"not configured is never a failure to alert on\" gate `mirror_failure` already has — so an instance that has not opted into ingestion never sees a spurious alert.\n- `POST /api/mail/poll`, bearer-token protected (`IMAP_POLL_CRON_TOKEN`), mirrors `/api/alerts/run/[job]` exactly: nothing in this repository schedules a pass itself, per AGENTS.md's \"future worker process\" gap. A production instance needs a cron entry, e.g. every 2–5 minutes:\n  ```\n  */3 * * * * curl -fsS -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $IMAP_POLL_CRON_TOKEN\" https://<host>/api/mail/poll\n  ```\n\n## Non-goals honoured\n\nDoes not read message content for extraction (only headers: `Message-ID`, `Subject`, `Date` — the same denormalized-header role `document.originalName` already plays, never interpreted). Does not decide local vs. hosted (#81) — that's #82/#85's job once a contract's `hosted_extraction_consent_document_id` exists. Does not build the runner.\n\n## Verified against a real GreenMail container (not a mock)\n\n`docker compose -f compose.mail-test.yaml up -d`, then `pnpm test -- src/lib/server/mail/poll.test.ts` (6 tests, all against real IMAP APPEND/UID/UIDVALIDITY):\n\n- A new message is picked up and handed off exactly once.\n- **Restart proof**: two independent, fully-committed `pollMailboxesOnce` calls (real Postgres commits, not a rolled-back test transaction — the second call reads nothing but what the first left in the database, exactly what a real process restart would also see) — the second call hands off nothing for the already-seen message, then a genuinely new message appended afterward is still picked up.\n- **UIDVALIDITY bump proof**: the mailbox is actually deleted and recreated (forcing GreenMail's real UIDVALIDITY to change, confirmed non-equal before/after), the same message is re-appended under the new generation, and it is *not* rehanded off, while a second, genuinely new message under the new generation is.\n- A folder that doesn't exist fails only that contract; another contract's folder in the same pass still gets its message handed off, and the run is recorded `failure` with the failing contract named in `detail`.\n- A connection to an unreachable port retries with backoff (asserted attempt count and backoff schedule via an injectable delay) and is recorded as a `failure` run with detail, not swallowed.\n- Nothing is attempted, and no run is recorded, when no contract has a folder configured.\n\n`pnpm lint`, `pnpm check`, `pnpm test` (twice, containers up throughout — nothing skipped besides the two pre-existing, unrelated fixtures this branch didn't touch: `caddy-xff.test.ts` and `dispatch.test.ts`, both gated on containers/env this PR has no reason to start), `pnpm build` all pass locally. CI dispatched on this branch.\n\n## What I could not verify\n\nI did not smoke-test the `/mail/contracts/[id]` folder-setting form or the `/api/mail/poll` route through a browser/built-server session — the automated test suite (schema constraints, repository queries, the full poll orchestration against real GreenMail, and `svelte-check`'s route-guard exhaustiveness test) covers the same paths without that extra pass, and I'm out of session budget to add it. Worth a manual look before merge if that matters to you.\n\n## Scope note\n\nI left `repositories/contract.ts`'s other functions (`listContracts`, `createContract`, etc.) untouched — they don't take a `DbExecutor`, unlike `document.ts`/`document-mirror.ts`'s convention. I only added `executor` threading to the two functions this feature actually composes transactionally (`listContractsWithMailFolder`), matching `listUnmirroredDocuments`'s own precedent, not a repo-wide cleanup."}